SOUNDDVR device-SELECT + OPL/AdLib device-3 INIT: reach the first real out(0x388) on the menu.

With patch 352 threading the SOUND.CFG letter 'C' into 014e -> device code 3, this patch reconstructs the
faithful driver-DS-rebased device-select + device-3 (OPL) init chain so the engine actually programs the
OPL chip (port 0x388/0x389 via the writer FUN_0000_0f21).  All are the MGAVIDEO-031-072 driver base-loss
class: every ds: access is to the driver's OWN data segment (DAT_0000_0831<<4 = load_seg+0x2a5), which
Ghidra rendered as engine-DGROUP DAT_1000_cNN / host-absolute derefs.  Asm-verified vs
re_out/fist_snd_image.bin:

  * 014e  - read the threaded music-device letter (bdcc/patch 352 published byte[DGROUP:0x248]='C').
  * 0872  - device-select: copy device 3's 7 method vectors from the per-device table driver_ds:0x17d..
            into the live slots driver_ds:0x17b.., then call slot0 = 104f (the OPL init).
  * 104f  - OPL init: 0f21(0x120/0x800/0xbdc0) global regs + 1082 + per-channel 0f99 key-off.
  * 1082  - program the 9 OPL channel level/key registers.
  * 0f99  - load a channel's OPL operator regs from the 16-byte instrument record driver_ds:(i*0x10+0x1dd).

The OPL writer FUN_0000_0f21 (asm 0xf21 = out 0x388,AH; delay; out 0x389,AL) is already faithful in the
re-decompile (no driver-DS state) -- it needs no rebase.

Reached only under FIST_SB (the DGROUP:0x508 config vector is FIST_SB-installed, patch 344/348); on the
default boot the config method is never dispatched -> zero effect on the 26 video flows.  fist_snd.c was
re-decompiled with the device-3 method seeds (0x872,0xa14,0xf21,0xf48,0xf54,0xf99,0x104f,0x1082,0x10a5,
0x10a6,0x10e3) -> new reproducible pristine md5 (docs/audio.md §13).
